%N A401274 a(n) is the smallest deficient number (A005100) that is equal to the sum of n distinct abundant numbers (A005101).
%C A401274 Offset is 2 because for n = 1, a number cannot be both abundant and deficient.
%C A401274 Similar to A401272, but for abundant numbers and to A401273, but for deficient numbers.
%e A401274 a(3) = 50 = A005100(39) = 12 + 18 + 20 = A005101(1) + A005101(2) + A005101(3).
%Y A401274 Cf. A005100, A005101, A401272, A401273.
%K A401274 nonn,new
%O A401274 2,1
